 "overall_low_pct": 2.7,
 "overall_high_pct": 20.3,
 "overall_method": "Low: 257 distinct attempts in all counted types over 9554 (ceilings, or floors where no ceiling exists). High: 226 distinct attempts over 1111 (floors), after leaving out five types that are mostly not attempts to found a place: special economic zones, Indigenous self-government, flag registers, new states and private cities. The same narrow group over its ceilings gives 9.0 percent. Because many ceilings are unknown, the true figures are lower. The other 128 attempts on the map are left out because no outside total was sought for them.",
 "reading": "The map is a selective record and does not match real-world proportions, so its charts show what has been documented here and not how common each route is. Counted against all types it holds about 3 percent of known real examples, and among attempts to found a place it holds about 9 to 20 percent. Micronations are the largest group at 96 of 385 attempts, a far higher share than their real weight beside the 479 self-determination movements since 1945, of which the map has 8. The most under-counted types are special economic zones (about 0.1 percent), Indigenous self-government (1.5), secessionist movements (1.7), flag registers (2.1) and new states (2.8), mainly because they are very numerous and most are not private attempts to found territory. Types with few real cases, such as private space stations and international zones, are covered far better, and one entry can bundle several cases."
